@startuml
' What: the five ego symptoms on the Unciv body (D-50).
' Shows: intensity per family = ego x temperament share; each family shows as one phenomenon with its Unciv form.
'        The player sees the phenomenon name, never the emotion (D-17).
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-40, D-50. Penalty sizes c_f are playtest values.
title Ego symptoms on the Unciv body (D-50)
rectangle "Profile\nintensity(f) = ego x temperament(f)" as P
rectangle "Waste\n- % Production and Food\n(larger cities more)" as W
rectangle "Unrest\n+ % Unhappiness\n(empire happiness)" as U
rectangle "We have nothing to learn\nknown-tech discount shrinks\n(hook: getScienceModifier)" as N
rectangle "Hoarding\n- % Gold from Trade Routes" as H
rectangle "Rivalry\n- % Science from research agreements,\nconnection bonus shrinks" as R
P --> W : Confusion
P --> U : Anger
P --> N : Pride
P --> H : Attachment
P --> R : Jealousy
note bottom of P : Injected each generation into temporaryUniques,\nphenomenon name as source name.\nPride and Jealousy do nothing to a realm alone.
@enduml
